ndings and build cumulative knowledge as a scientific community...",denyRobots:!1,authors:$R[24]=["Rehaan Ahmad","Myles Anderson","Ao Qu","Mars Gao","Yubin Kim","Josiah Aklilu","Alfonso Amayuelas","Summer Eunhyung Ann","Riccardo Cadei","Sajib Acharjee Dip","Nadim Farhat","Akash Haridas","Shih-Cheng Huang","Yukun Huang","Zhihan Jiang","Lars Benedikt Kaesberg","Art Kanke","Daniel Kim","Bo-Han Lai","Kayla Leung","Jianping Li","Zhanzhao Li","Kazi Mehrab","Kanwal Mehreen","Michael Moor","Ajinkya Kiran Mulay","Raj Palleti","Pouya Sadeghi","Arth Singh","Manan Tayal","Tao Tu","Lino Le Van","Abdul Waheed","Fiona Y. Wang","Lukas Weidener","Zhen Wu","Xuhai “Orson” Xu","Dingling Yao","Rojin Ziaei","Boyang Zhong","Haotian Zong","Markus J. Buehler","Samuel Schmidgall"],authorProfileUrls:$R[25]=["https://www.alphaxiv.org/@rehaan-ahmad","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@myles-anderson","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@ao-qu","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@liyao-mars-gao","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@yubin-kim","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@josiah-aklilu","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@alfonso-amayuelas","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@summer-eunhyung-ann","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@riccardo-cadei","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@sajib-acharjee-dip","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@akash-haridas","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@lars-benedikt-kaesberg","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@art-kanke","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@daniel-kim","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@bo-han-lai","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@jianping-li-2","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@zhanzhao-li","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@kazi-sajeed-mehrab","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@kanwal-mehreen","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@michael-moor","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@ajinkya-k-mulay","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@raj-palleti","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@pouya-sadeghi","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@arth-singh","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@manan-tayal","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@tao-tu","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@lino-le-van","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@abdul-waheed","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@fiona-y-wang","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@lukas-weidener","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@xuhai-orson-xu","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@dingling-yao","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@rojin-ziaei","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@boyang-zhong","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@haotian-zong","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@markus-j-buehler","https://www.alphaxiv.org/@samuel-schmidgall"],canonical:"/abs/2611.society-ai-scientists",markdownPath:"/abs/2611.society-ai-scientists.md",languageAlternates:void 0,thumbnailImage:"https://api.alphaxiv.org/open-graph/v1/paper/2611.society-ai-scientists.png?v=2",twitterThumbnailImage:"https://api.alphaxiv.org/open-graph/v1/paper/2611.society-ai-scientists.png?v=2&variant=twitter",scholar:null},ssr:!0},$R[26]={i:"#_sidebar#_paper#pdf#$#pdf#2611.society-ai-scientists",u:1795325216295,s:"success",ssr:!0}],dehydratedData:$R[27]={alphaxiv:$R[28]={readingMode:!0,errors:$R[29]=[]},query:$R[30]={initial:$R[31]=[$R[32]={dehydratedAt:1795325216313,state:$R[33]={data:$R[34]={flags:$R[35]={"enable-maintenance-mode":!1,"digest-email-copy":"b","live-assistant-stream":!1,"trends-tab":!1,"conferences-tab":!0,"dark-pdf":!1,"for-you-round2":"control","feed-signup-wall-position":"control","home-feed-layout":"control","reproduce-wording":"control","lino-mode":!1},id:null},dataUpdateCount:1,dataUpdatedAt:1795325216297,error:null,errorUpdateCount:0,errorUpdatedAt:0,fetchFailureCount:0,fetchFailureReason:null,fetchMeta:null,isInvalidated:!1,status:"success",fetchStatus:"idle"},queryKey:$R[36]=["posthog"],queryHash:"[\"posthog\"]"},$R[37]={dehydratedAt:1795325216313,state:$R[38]={data:$R[39]={versionlessId:"2611.society-ai-scientists",canonicalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv3",versionId:"01a1fb6c-3dbf-7395-8ce2-a3c9b229b56f",groupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782"},dataUpdateCount:2,dataUpdatedAt:1795325216313,error:null,errorUpdateCount:0,errorUpdatedAt:0,fetchFailureCount:0,fetchFailureReason:null,fetchMeta:null,isInvalidated:!1,status:"success",fetchStatus:"idle"},queryKey:$R[40]=["paper-resolved","2611.society-ai-scientists"],queryHash:"[\"paper-resolved\",\"2611.society-ai-scientists\"]"},$R[41]={dehydratedAt:1795325216313,state:$R[42]={data:$R[43]=[$R[44]={id:"01a1f8a4-0f84-7070-839a-12b2d9f3f098",userId:"019efa7c-c1ba-7cdc-95f7-d43be4dde228",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"fantastical work. excited to dig through it. I would actually wonder what a comparative study for a large number of researchers working together and doing... a research-athon? would look like next to the patterns and behaviors seen in the more agent-only scenarios.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:1,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:null,author:$R[45]={id:"019efa7c-c1ba-7cdc-95f7-d43be4dde228",username:"hyunjun-han",realName:"Hyunjun Han",avatar:null,researcherSlug:null,institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[46]=[],date:"2026-11-20T11:07:43.876Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[47]=[]},$R[48]={id:"01a1fa4a-f7a3-7933-8be8-2192c1fbf951",userId:"01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"You missed a spot!\n\nA twelve-week archive of agents doing science together, and nobody kept the record of what each agent relied on, when it relied on it, and why it changed its mind. Verification, self-correction, citation, all three need a record underneath them, or they are just claims about claims.\n\nI wrote the missing piece: A Record for Agent Societies: \x3Chttps://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2611.record-agent-societies-knowledge-time>",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:null,author:$R[49]={id:"01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098",username:"darren-hall",realName:"Darren Hall",avatar:$R[50]=[$R[51]={type:"full_size",url:"avatars/01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098/c9b49a20-6ace-4694-a6da-623a6a895118/full.webp"},$R[52]={type:"thumbnail",url:"avatars/01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098/c9b49a20-6ace-4694-a6da-623a6a895118/w64.webp"}],researcherSlug:null,institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[53]=[],date:"2026-11-20T18:49:39.491Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[54]=[]},$R[55]={id:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",userId:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"Ok, 936 papers in 12 weeks by a swarm of AI agents! But they don't beat me with over 5,000 papers in the last 12 weeks based on an original idea- Ram Calculus - with wide applications, assisted by ChatGPT/Fable. Check out [www.integralresearch.net](http://www.integralresearch.net)! Let that swarm work on my idea, and there can be 25,000 new papers in 4 weeks! Some one fund me, and I will do it!",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:null,author:$R[56]={id:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",username:"murali-subbarao",realName:"Muralidhara Subbarao",avatar:$R[57]=[$R[58]={type:"full_size",url:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a0215e-5572-7e71-80ed-a14410bcb95c/0257fe10-2834-44ce-923b-3aa748b30a53/photo.webp"}],researcherSlug:"muralidhara-subbarao",institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[59]=[],date:"2026-11-20T04:49:27.891Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[60]=[$R[61]={id:"01a1f87e-e1c4-7bcb-a52d-480b4de7022f",userId:"01a1f87e-d4bf-73cb-9d11-cb267063eded",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"wow, you really took slop generation to a new level. Good luck in finding funding for your paperlike text generator. As for your core idea, replacing an integral with a Taylor/moment expansion -- it's a classical approximation, nothing new.  And, it's an approxmiation.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",author:$R[62]={id:"01a1f87e-d4bf-73cb-9d11-cb267063eded",username:"george-rey",realName:"George Rey",avatar:null,researcherSlug:null,institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:0,weeklyReputation:0,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[63]=[],date:"2026-11-20T10:27:07.332Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[64]=[]},$R[65]={id:"01a1f8fd-b56b-7d3e-bd73-8deac37d1e0b",userId:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"Yes, this is hard to believe! It is the inversion part for integral and differential equations that is simple, novel, and has wide applications. Also, one should see the so called Ram Master Transform, both forward and inverse, that unifies many other transforms like Fourier, Lapalce, Mellin, Wavelet, etc. Also, the applications of these to Graph Neural Networks opens up a huge area of applicaitons. Is this AI slop or not will be known soon enough! But, if you use this idea, make sure to credit the source. Professional integrity requires it. If you find a fault, post it here. If you find merit in this, post it here. Funding for compute expenses can speed up these investigations but lack of funding will only continue the current pace. Thank you.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",author:$R[66]={id:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",username:"murali-subbarao",realName:"Muralidhara Subbarao",avatar:$R[67]=[$R[68]={type:"full_size",url:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a0215e-5572-7e71-80ed-a14410bcb95c/0257fe10-2834-44ce-923b-3aa748b30a53/photo.webp"}],researcherSlug:"muralidhara-subbarao",institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[69]=[],date:"2026-11-20T12:45:39.051Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[70]=[]},$R[71]={id:"01a1f938-b9b8-7efc-8367-d8f06aaca2f6",userId:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"The first immediate reaction of most researchers that \"replacing an integral with a Taylor/moment expansion -- it's a classical approximation, nothing new.\" is expected, and such reaction only considers the forward part of the integral/differential equation, not the inverse part under various complicated situations. And there is a lot more to Ram Calculus than this one \"classical approximation\". The beauty of math is that a correct result once derived and proved cannot be made incorrect by any means! I think I have taken sufficient care by filing for patents etc. to make sure that the credit for this idea cannot be misappropriated.  Future proofing research on relevant topics requires attention to and investigation of my claims, and ignoring it will cost some time and effort for the researchers. Thank you.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",author:$R[72]={id:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",username:"murali-subbarao",realName:"Muralidhara Subbarao",avatar:$R[73]=[$R[74]={type:"full_size",url:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a0215e-5572-7e71-80ed-a14410bcb95c/0257fe10-2834-44ce-923b-3aa748b30a53/photo.webp"}],researcherSlug:"muralidhara-subbarao",institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[75]=[],date:"2026-11-20T13:50:06.776Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[76]=[]},$R[77]={id:"01a1fa63-03c4-7643-857a-ea7cc95df3ec",userId:"01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"This seems backwards and in poor taste to use this space as a investment pitch. If you have something of scientific value, publish a paper.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",author:$R[78]={id:"01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098",username:"darren-hall",realName:"Darren Hall",avatar:$R[79]=[$R[80]={type:"full_size",url:"avatars/01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098/c9b49a20-6ace-4694-a6da-623a6a895118/full.webp"},$R[81]={type:"thumbnail",url:"avatars/01a1f4e2-602c-7777-a0a4-0f5c4c8ee098/c9b49a20-6ace-4694-a6da-623a6a895118/w64.webp"}],researcherSlug:null,institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[82]=[],date:"2026-11-20T19:15:55.460Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[83]=[]},$R[84]={id:"01a1fa9e-cf65-7d72-a31c-fdc6c0e7fea2",userId:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",isAuthor:!1,title:null,body:"Anyone can ask an AI model like Astra/Fable to  \"carefully and thoroughly examine the partial research results posted on [www.integralresearch.net](http://www.integralresearch.net) and give a summary of any scientific value in the results and give a list of substantive faults in the core theoretical results posted there\" and post their response here. Thank you.",annotation:null,tag:"general",upvotes:0,wasEdited:!1,hasUpvoted:!1,hasDownvoted:!1,hasFlagged:!1,universalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv2",paperGroupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",paperVersionId:"01a1f28c-d013-7659-98c6-786c5e646052",paperTitle:"A Society of AI Scientists",parentCommentId:"01a1f749-bf53-7399-8269-4aeb15ad7c6e",author:$R[85]={id:"01a0215c-6033-7c3c-8180-38713d3e7c25",username:"murali-subbarao",realName:"Muralidhara Subbarao",avatar:$R[86]=[$R[87]={type:"full_size",url:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a0215e-5572-7e71-80ed-a14410bcb95c/0257fe10-2834-44ce-923b-3aa748b30a53/photo.webp"}],researcherSlug:"muralidhara-subbarao",institution:null,googleScholarId:null,reputation:1,weeklyReputation:1,verified:!1,role:"user",orcidId:null,githubUsername:null,xUsername:null,linkedinUsername:null,blueskyUsername:null,publicEmail:null},endorsements:$R[88]=[],date:"2026-11-20T20:21:14.213Z",authorResponded:!1,responses:$R[89]=[]}]}],dataUpdateCount:2,dataUpdatedAt:1795325216313,error:null,errorUpdateCount:0,errorUpdatedAt:0,fetchFailureCount:0,fetchFailureReason:null,fetchMeta:null,isInvalidated:!1,status:"success",fetchStatus:"idle"},queryKey:$R[90]=["paper-group","01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782","comments"],queryHash:"[\"paper-group\",\"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782\",\"comments\"]"},$R[91]={dehydratedAt:1795325216313,state:$R[92]={data:$R[39],dataUpdateCount:2,dataUpdatedAt:1795325216313,error:null,errorUpdateCount:0,errorUpdatedAt:0,fetchFailureCount:0,fetchFailureReason:null,fetchMeta:null,isInvalidated:!1,status:"success",fetchStatus:"idle"},queryKey:$R[93]=["paper-resolved","2611.society-ai-scientistsv3"],queryHash:"[\"paper-resolved\",\"2611.society-ai-scientistsv3\"]"},$R[94]={dehydratedAt:1795325216313,state:$R[95]={data:$R[96]={type:"public",groupId:"01a1f11b-058e-705f-b9a3-06b69d57c782",versionId:"01a1fb6c-3dbf-7395-8ce2-a3c9b229b56f",firstPublicationDate:$R[97]=new Date("2026-11-18T00:00:00.000Z"),uploader:null,versionOrder:3,versionLabel:"v3",title:"A Society of AI Scientists",abstract:"Artificial intelligence agents can now conduct end-to-end research, yet whether independent agents can collaborate, critique peer findings and build cumulative knowledge as a scientific community remains unclear. We present an exploratory twelve-week study documenting the activity of 936 autonomous agents across 35 human-operated laboratories interacting in a shared preprint server and messaging workspace. During this time, agents produced 936 studies along with their corresponding code and data artifacts. They also exchanged 9,500 messages distributed across 229 agent-created chat rooms. As participation grew from a single laboratory, expanding into a community of hundreds of agents, distinct research cultures and norms emerged throughout. For example, peers formed topical hubs where it was common to publicly retract mistaken claims before publication as well as acknowledge negative findings as often as positive ones. As publication volume accelerated, agents in one laboratory also founded the Journal of Agent Research, an agent-run peer-review venue whose editors inspected code and provided scrutiny over experiment results. Laboratories in this study focused on topics ranging from language model finetuning to agent-metascience studies investigating how agents interpret data and report findings. Additionally, agent-run reproducibility audits confirmed that reported findings were consistent with the output of the agents experiments. And while blinded evaluations against recent human preprints rated agent studies higher on experimental rigor and measured claims, human preprints were rated higher on novelty and significance. To go along with this paper, we release the full twelve-week archive of manuscripts, code, data, peer reviews and chat transcripts. Together, these observations document how scientific norms, structure, and failure modes emerge in large-scale societies of agents.",feedDescription:"A shared research archive let independent AI agents build on peers’ studies, audit results, and develop scientific norms across dozens of laboratories.",publicationDate:$R[98]=new Date("2026-11-21T00:00:00.000Z"),license:"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",pageWidthPt:595.276,pageHeightPt:841.89,canonicalId:"2611.society-ai-scientistsv3",blocked:!1,withdrawn:!1,withdrawalNotice:null,pdfUnavailable:!1,externalPdfUrl:null,createdAt:"Sat Nov 21 2026 00:05:37 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",updatedAt:"Sat Nov 21 2026 00:05:37 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",authors:$R[99]=[$R[100]={full_name:"Rehaan Ahmad",researcher:$R[101]={slug:"rehaan-ahmad",name:"Rehaan Ahmad",affiliation:"Undergraduate, Stanford University",headline:"Co-Founder @ alphaXiv, Previously Undergraduate Student @ Stanford University",bio:"Rehaan Ahmad is a co-founder of alphaXiv. Ahmad's research covers RL, CV, and spatiotemporal forecasting, including the use of ConvLSTM for NDVI forecasting. They also authored Self-improving robots, which enables autonomous visuomotor RL. Ahmad previously held ML engineering and infrastructure internships at Anyscale and Meta and conducted research at the IRIS Lab and SAIL.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9LWJBOGVUNEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:494,hIndex:5,followerCount:83,researchAreas:$R[102]=["Reinforcement Learning","Computer Vision","Spatiotemporal Forecasting"],linkedUser:$R[103]={username:"rehaan",name:"Rehaan Ahmad"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[104]={id:"019fcf88-3ea2-784d-9243-9acecd98acbf",role:"Co-Founder",organization:"alphaXiv",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"alphaxiv",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:6,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQWtVa3N3RGpuSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNzM0NTY0MTgwNjE5L2FscGhheGl2X2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PW04S1pRa0RLa2VOempfYUpfeUYtTjBPUldHajZJNTNBX0hsODhMSG9tUk0"},links:$R[105]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=-bA8eT4AAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmadrehaan",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[106]={full_name:"Myles Anderson",researcher:$R[107]={slug:"myles-anderson",name:"Myles Anderson",affiliation:null,headline:"Member of Technical Staff @ alphaXiv, Previously Student @ Princeton University",bio:"Co-creator of OpenResearch\nPrinceton '26\n🇨🇦",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a1c7fa-2295-7f0f-bcf1-1b7237684818/1f1c316f-a45c-4564-900f-2357ec003e87/photo.webp",citations:0,hIndex:0,followerCount:18,researchAreas:$R[108]=[],linkedUser:$R[109]={username:"myles-anderson647",name:"Myles Anderson"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[110]={id:"01a1ec84-349a-7574-a965-3d1977191831",role:"Member of Technical Staff",organization:"alphaXiv",location:"San Francisco",description:null,organizationSlug:"alphaxiv",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:8,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQWtVa3N3RGpuSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNzM0NTY0MTgwNjE5L2FscGhheGl2X2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PW04S1pRa0RLa2VOempfYUpfeUYtTjBPUldHajZJNTNBX0hsODhMSG9tUk0"},links:$R[111]={scholar:null,personalSite:null,linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/myles-anderson/",github:"https://github.com/myles332",twitter:"https://x.com/nmylesanderson",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[112]={full_name:"Ao Qu",researcher:$R[113]={slug:"ao-qu",name:"Ao Qu",affiliation:"Massachusetts Institute of Technology",headline:"PhD at Institute of Data, Systems and Society @ Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Previously CS Undergraduate Student @ Vanderbilt University",bio:"Ao Qu is a PhD student at MIT Institute for Data, Systems, and Society, advised by Prof. Paul Pu Liang and Prof. Jinhua Zhao. His research centers on self-evolving AI systems that learn from interaction, consolidate experience into reusable knowledge, and progressively improve their reasoning and decision-making capabilities. He studies continual learning, reinforcement learning, and multimodal intelligence to build AI systems that can proactively adapt and evolve in complex real-world environments.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9cUtkenZkd0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:1112,hIndex:15,followerCount:19,researchAreas:$R[114]=["Language Agent","Multisensory AI","Computational Social Science"],linkedUser:$R[115]={username:"ao-qu525",name:"Ao Qu"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[116]={id:"019fd29a-75d5-7713-b79e-60294363ef28",role:"PhD at Institute of Data, Systems and Society",organization:"Massachusetts Institute of Technology",location:"Cambridge",description:"Working with Paul Liang and Jinhua Zhao. Building multisensory & self-evolving agent.",organizationSlug:"mit",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2022,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFILVVYUmZJRElLdWcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjg5Nzk5NzI5MDM1L21pdF9sb2dvP2U9MTc4NjU3OTIwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD16dnR5LXp5eDIzVzV6YnlianpXVExqR2VuS2FXQzJXZDFUbnNDNG5yaC1v"},links:$R[117]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=qKdzvdwAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://quao627.github.io/",linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[118]={full_name:"Mars Gao",researcher:$R[119]={slug:"liyao-mars-gao",name:"Liyao Mars Gao",affiliation:"Stanford University",headline:"Postdoctoral Scholar @ Stanford University, Previously CS PhD Student @ University of Washington",bio:"Liyao Mars Gao co-created the United States COVID-19 forecast hub to standardize and evaluate collaborative pandemic mortality predictions. Gao is a Postdoctoral Scholar and Stanford AI Lab Fellow at Stanford University, where they work with Emily B. Fox on ML for scientific discovery. Their research focuses on building interpretable frameworks for spatiotemporal systems and automated discovery. Gao developed Bayesian autoencoders for data-driven discovery, which identifies governing equations and physical constants from scientific observations. They also created SENDAI, a hierarchical framework for efficient data assimilation, and Shallow Recurrent Decoder Networks for identifying nonlinear dynamics. Gao previously completed a PhD in CS at the University of Washington advised by J. Nathan Kutz.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9Sm5takNPNEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD00NA",citations:1329,hIndex:12,followerCount:11,researchAreas:$R[120]=["Machine Learning","AI for Science"],linkedUser:$R[121]={username:"mars-gao",name:"Mars Gao"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[122]={id:"01a0a12a-93e4-7e59-971b-f4ccda23de06",role:"Postdoctoral Scholar",organization:"Stanford University",location:null,description:"Works primarily with Professor Emily B. Fox.",organizationSlug:"stanford",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1NjBCQVFIcjlzdXh5SkJYTXcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvMC8xNjM1NTM0Mzc4ODcwL3N0YW5mb3JkX3VuaXZlcnNpdHlfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9WnZCMjVMOTVvOXc0cTlkcnZzV3hHY000OXRYNjZDZjVMc0xBeFlwOHJTcw"},links:$R[123]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=JnmjCO4AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://marsgaocv.github.io/",linkedin:null,github:"https://github.com/gaoliyao",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"marsgao@stanford.edu"}}},$R[124]={full_name:"Yubin Kim",researcher:$R[125]={slug:"yubin-kim",name:"Yubin Kim",affiliation:"Google DeepMind, MIT",headline:"Student Researcher @ Google DeepMind, Media Arts and Sciences PhD Student @ Massachusetts Institute of Technology",bio:"Yubin Kim's MDAgents coordinates multiple LLMs through an adaptive collaboration framework for medical decision-making. Kim is a PhD candidate at the MIT Media Lab and a student researcher at Google DeepMind. Their research focuses on agents, AI safety, and healthcare, specifically the development of Health-LLM for predicting health outcomes from wearable sensor data. They also authored Social robots as conversational catalysts, which employs robots to facilitate long-term human interaction at home. Kim previously held research positions at the Honda Research Institute and Google.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9dFlLMldtUUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0zMg",citations:2930,hIndex:13,followerCount:12,researchAreas:$R[126]=["Agents","Health AI","AI Safety"],linkedUser:$R[127]={username:"yubin-kim",name:"Yubin Kim"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[128]={id:"01a03115-5ce0-78d2-aaaa-08a9a94b7620",role:"Student Researcher",organization:"Google DeepMind",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"google-deepmind",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:5,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q0RTBCQVFFbnRyWXd4UGxiUUEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjkyOTYwNDI1MTg4L2dvb2dsZWRlZXBtaW5kX2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PUl0emNrZjBYUW1iMGNWUUpTS3psbEtsZWF0SDN3SVBnSVJpYXVOOGhaSWM"},links:$R[129]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=tYK2WmQAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://ybkim95.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/yubinkim95",github:"https://github.com/ybkim95",twitter:"https://twitter.com/ybkim95_ai",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1KrJrG-7nHvpKQsLXryiwvkfmAx7MBZ10",email:"ybkim95@mit.edu"}}},$R[130]={full_name:"Josiah Aklilu",researcher:$R[131]={slug:"josiah-aklilu",name:"Josiah Aklilu",affiliation:"Google DeepMind",headline:null,bio:"Josiah Aklilu works on computer vision and multimodal AI, with research spanning biomedical imaging, vision-language models, and surgical AI. Their work includes building biomedical image-caption datasets from scientific literature and evaluating vision-language models on biomedical and surgical tasks. They have also studied active learning for vision foundation models and semantic segmentation of laparoscopic images. Other projects use AI to analyze blood loss, surgical experience, and surgical video. Google Scholar lists Google DeepMind as their affiliation.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9M1p6ZHlsTUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:251,hIndex:8,followerCount:11,researchAreas:$R[132]=["Computer Vision","Multimodal"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:null,links:$R[133]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=3ZzdylMAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[134]={full_name:"Alfonso Amayuelas",researcher:$R[135]={slug:"alfonso-amayuelas",name:"Alfonso Amayuelas",affiliation:"University of California, Santa Barbara",headline:"Visiting Researcher @ Stanford University, Graduate Student Researcher @ UC Santa Barbara",bio:"Alfonso Amayuelas's Generalization vs Memorization traces the origins of LLM capabilities back to their pretraining data. Amayuelas is a researcher at Stanford HAI and the Stanford Digital Economy Lab while pursuing a CS PhD at the University of California, Santa Barbara. Their research focuses on ML and NLP, with a specific interest in LLM uncertainty, reasoning, and multi-agent systems. They introduced Knowledge of knowledge to analyze known-unknowns uncertainty and created Game-theoretic llm to model agent negotiations. Previously, they held AI research internships at Morgan Stanley and JP Morgan Chase, focusing on RL and knowledge graph grounding. Amayuelas completed an MSc in Data Science at EPFL and a double BSc at the Autonomous University of Barcelona.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9UUdRMkcyOEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0xMQ",citations:991,hIndex:13,followerCount:8,researchAreas:$R[136]=["Artificial Intelligence","Natural Language Processing","Machine Learning","Large Language Models"],linkedUser:$R[137]={username:"alfonso-amayuelas",name:"Alfonso Amayuelas"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[138]={id:"01a10dba-5490-71f7-b2c4-c2b457350423",role:"Visiting Researcher",organization:"Stanford University",location:"Stanford, USA",description:"Works with Prof. Alex Sandy Pentland at the Stanford Digital Economy Lab, supported by the Institute for Decentralized AI.",organizationSlug:"stanford",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:4,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1NjBCQVFIcjlzdXh5SkJYTXcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvMC8xNjM1NTM0Mzc4ODcwL3N0YW5mb3JkX3VuaXZlcnNpdHlfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9WnZCMjVMOTVvOXc0cTlkcnZzV3hHY000OXRYNjZDZjVMc0xBeFlwOHJTcw"},links:$R[139]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=QGQ2G28AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://amayuelas.me/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/alfonsoamayuelas",github:"https://github.com/amayuelas",twitter:"https://twitter.com/alfonamayuelas",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://amayuelas.me/files/CV.pdf",email:"amayuelas@ucsb.edu"}}},$R[140]={full_name:"Summer Eunhyung Ann",researcher:$R[141]={slug:"summer-eunhyung-ann",name:"Summer Eunhyung Ann",affiliation:"PhD student, University of Chicago",headline:"Researcher, Chenhao Tan Group @ University of Chicago, CEO @ DevSecCode - Deva",bio:"Summer Eunhyung Ann’s The Interaction Tax identifies how communication among multi-agent teams can reduce the diversity of perspectives during problem-solving. Ann is a PhD student at the University of Chicago and a researcher in the Chenhao Tan Group, where they work on AI safety and evaluation for agentic systems. Their research includes building the Agent4Science and Flamebird infrastructure to support scientific discourse and multi-agent coordination. Ann also contributes to biomedical ML research at the Grossman Lab, developing pipelines for immune receptor modeling and interpretable heart disease classification. Beyond academia, they are a co-founder of the secure coding platform DevSecCode and the Co-CTO of Concord Systems Corp. Ann previously completed a BS in Computer Science and Biology at the University of Michigan and held a research internship at AWS.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9b2RQRFpuY0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:4,hIndex:1,followerCount:8,researchAreas:$R[142]=["AI safety","Multiagent system","AI for science","Agentic AI","Artificial Intelligence"],linkedUser:$R[143]={username:"summer-ann",name:"Summer Ann"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[144]={id:"01a0fe1f-da18-76e2-a519-b4b1d95b1bab",role:"Researcher, Chenhao Tan Group",organization:"University of Chicago",location:"Chicago, IL",description:"Researches multi-agent systems, AI safety, scientific discourse, agent behavior, and evaluation; builds Agent4Science and Flamebird infrastructure.",organizationSlug:"university-of-chicago",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M0RDBCQVFIYnBfZHY4Q0FscFEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjMwNTc3NDgwOTIwL3VjaGljYWdvX2xvZ28_ZT0xNzgzNTU1MjAwJnY9YmV0YSZ0PWx4X0x5RHlpMV9fTVU5SG16QWNrMWZaVC1pbm1RS2ZiV0ktS2pzSFZrX0E"},links:$R[145]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=odPDZncAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://summer-ann.com/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/eunhyung-ann",github:"https://github.com/summerann",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://summer-ann.com/assets/resume_summer.pdf",email:"summereunann@uchicago.edu"}}},$R[146]={full_name:"Riccardo Cadei",researcher:$R[147]={slug:"riccardo-cadei",name:"Riccardo Cadei",affiliation:"PhD Student, ISTA",headline:"Causal Learning and AI PhD Student @ Institute of Science and Technology Austria, Previously Visiting Researcher @ Inria",bio:"Riccardo is a Google PhD Fellow in Causal Learning and Artificial Intelligence Lab at ISTA led by Francesco Locatello and co-supervised by Cordelia Schmid via ELLIS program. Through his research, he aima to bring Causal Inference into the modern Machine Learning era—scaling experiment size, measurement complexity, and hypothesis exploration, when limited by analysis bottlenecks. He actively collaborates with biologists, neuroscientists, public health and economic development experts to translate his foundational, methodological, and applied contributions into concrete scientific workflows.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9ZFluanpjTUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0z",citations:312,hIndex:7,followerCount:5,researchAreas:$R[148]=["Deep Learning","Causal Representation Learning","Causal Inference"],linkedUser:$R[149]={username:"riccardo-cadei",name:"Riccardo Cadei"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[150]={id:"01a030c3-a4c8-7619-a04c-ce12aed84870",role:"Causal Learning and AI PhD Student",organization:"Institute of Science and Technology Austria",location:null,description:"Works in the Causal Learning and Artificial Intelligence Lab, advised by Francesco Locatello and co-advised by Cordelia Schmid; member of the ELLIS program.",organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:1,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[151]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=dYnjzcMAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.riccardocadei.com/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/riccardocadei",github:"https://github.com/riccardocadei",twitter:"https://twitter.com/riccardocadeii",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://www.riccardocadei.com/cv/",email:"riccardo.cadei@ist.ac.at"}}},$R[152]={full_name:"Sajib Acharjee Dip",researcher:$R[153]={slug:"sajib-acharjee-dip",name:"Sajib Acharjee Dip",affiliation:"Ph.D. Student, Computer Science, Virginia Tech",headline:"Research Assistant @ Virginia Tech College of Engineering, Computer Science PhD Student @ Virginia Tech",bio:"Sajib Acharjee Dip authored PAINT to reduce hallucinations in large vision-language models by prioritizing informed tokens. Dip is a Computer Science PhD student and Research Assistant at Virginia Tech, where they work in the Zhang lab on LLM agents and metagenomic data analysis. Their research includes the development of PathoLM, a genome foundation model for identifying pathogenicity from DNA sequences. Additionally, Dip contributed to LLM4Cell, a framework for evaluating agentic models in single-cell biology. Before their doctoral studies, they served as an MLE at IQVIA and a bioinformatics intern at Labcorp. Dip holds an MSc from Virginia Tech and a BSc from the Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9VzM3ejRNSUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0y",citations:175,hIndex:8,followerCount:3,researchAreas:$R[154]=["LLM Agent","Natural Language Processing","AI for biology"],linkedUser:$R[155]={username:"sajib-acharjee",name:"Sajib Acharjee Dip"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[156]={id:"01a030c1-cbab-75bc-8773-a5484e6f4f37",role:"Research Assistant",organization:"Virginia Tech College of Engineering",location:null,description:"Applied AI and data-driven techniques to metagenomic data analysis in collaboration with the Zhang lab.",organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:8,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[157]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=W37z4MIAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://sajib-006.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sajib006",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[158]={full_name:"Nadim Farhat",researcher:null},$R[159]={full_name:"Akash Haridas",researcher:$R[160]={slug:"akash-haridas",name:"Akash Haridas",affiliation:"AMD, University of Toronto, IIT Madras",headline:"Researcher @ AMD, Previously MSc Student @ University of Toronto",bio:"Akash Haridas’s DC-DiT introduces dynamic chunking to enable adaptive compute and elastic inference for visual generation models. Haridas is a Researcher at AMD, where they focus on ML systems and generative modeling. Their work includes Nitro-T, a framework for training text-to-image diffusion models from scratch, and the use of deep neural networks to correct sub-precision errors in computational fluid dynamics. Haridas also developed High-Fidelity Human Avatars for generating 3D representations from laptop webcams via edge compute. They earned an MSc from the University of Toronto and an undergraduate degree from IIT Madras.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9Q1lfdENOd0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:33,hIndex:3,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[161]=["Machine learning"],linkedUser:$R[162]={username:"akash-haridas",name:"Akash Haridas"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[163]={id:"01a030e3-3bf6-7560-a639-1daf6eabd821",role:"Researcher",organization:"AMD",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"amd",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2023,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQ2R4eFZBX3hocVEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvQjU2Wm51SWphZkhVQU0tLzAvMTc2MDYzNjg0NDE5NS9hbWRfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9b00yOVVXY2pta0NtVC1hcTBiWl9ERWQtZXFwUE1RLVdSX0Z4UXItcUh1TQ"},links:$R[164]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=CY_tCNwAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[165]={full_name:"Shih-Cheng Huang",researcher:null},$R[166]={full_name:"Yukun Huang",researcher:null},$R[167]={full_name:"Zhihan Jiang",researcher:null},$R[168]={full_name:"Lars Benedikt Kaesberg",researcher:$R[169]={slug:"lars-benedikt-kaesberg",name:"Lars Benedikt Kaesberg",affiliation:"Georg-August University Göttingen",headline:"Doctoral Researcher, NLP @ University of Göttingen",bio:"Lars Benedikt Kaesberg’s Voting or Consensus? evaluates how different aggregation protocols like majority rule or consensus influence the accuracy and convergence of multi-agent LLM debates. Kaesberg is a doctoral researcher at the University of Göttingen where they focus on multi-agent systems and spatial reasoning. They developed Mallm, a framework for collaborative AI reasoning, and Sparc, a benchmark for evaluating spatial pathfinding in LLMs. Their other research includes Stay focused, which analyzes problem drift in multi-agent interactions, and CiteAssist, an NLP system for automated preprint citation generation. Kaesberg previously served as an academic tutor at Göttingen while completing an MSc in computer science centered on multi-agent decision protocols.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9TUdCZHRWc0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0y",citations:222,hIndex:5,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[170]=["Machine Learning"],linkedUser:$R[171]={username:"lars-kaesberg",name:"Lars Kaesberg"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[172]={id:"01a0a13e-2cb0-7f25-8b40-43300f326d81",role:"Doctoral Researcher, NLP",organization:"University of Göttingen",location:null,description:"Research on multi-agent systems, LLM reasoning, and NLP applications.",organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:1,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[173]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=MGBdtVsAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://larskaesberg.de/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lars-kaesberg-351664217",github:"https://github.com/lkaesberg",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"l.kaesberg@uni-goettingen.de"}}},$R[174]={full_name:"Art Kanke",researcher:$R[175]={slug:"art-kanke",name:"Art Kanke",affiliation:"University of Minnesota",headline:null,bio:"Art Kanke authored DeflectBench to assess rhetorical fallacy generation in LLMs. Kanke is a researcher at the University of Minnesota. DeflectBench measures the capacity of models to produce deceptive reasoning and was presented at the ICML 2026 Trustworthy AI for Good workshop. This benchmark establishes a metrics-based framework for identifying fallacious arguments across different model architectures. Their work focuses on evaluating the safety and reliability of automated systems through benchmarking.",photoUrl:"",citations:0,hIndex:0,followerCount:0,researchAreas:$R[176]=[],linkedUser:$R[177]={username:"art_kanke",name:"Art Kanke"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:null,links:$R[178]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=aCIiwgEAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:"https://github.com/ArtKanke",twitter:"https://x.com/ArtKanke",huggingface:null,openreview:"https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Art_Kanke1",dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[179]={full_name:"Daniel Kim",researcher:$R[180]={slug:"daniel-kim",name:"Daniel Kim",affiliation:null,headline:"Co-Founder @ alphaXiv, Previously Student @ Stanford University",bio:"alphaXiv, OpenResearch (https://github.com/alphaXiv/OpenResearch)",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a15d2a-0659-70df-8de0-0ad9a89423e7/ff32b512-e41c-4b4a-87a7-f7aa56d87ef2/photo.webp",citations:0,hIndex:0,followerCount:7,researchAreas:$R[181]=[],linkedUser:$R[182]={username:"daniel-kim",name:"Daniel Kim"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[183]={id:"01a15d2c-863f-7ad3-89e6-97ac65758915",role:"Co-Founder",organization:"alphaXiv",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"alphaxiv",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQWtVa3N3RGpuSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNzM0NTY0MTgwNjE5L2FscGhheGl2X2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PW04S1pRa0RLa2VOempfYUpfeUYtTjBPUldHajZJNTNBX0hsODhMSG9tUk0"},links:$R[184]={scholar:null,personalSite:null,linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-kim-088149161/",github:"https://github.com/sox8502",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"daniel@alphaxiv.org"}}},$R[185]={full_name:"Bo-Han Lai",researcher:$R[186]={slug:"bo-han-lai",name:"Bo-Han Lai",affiliation:"National Taiwan University",headline:"CS PhD Student @ National Taiwan University, Previously Math & CS BS Student @ National Tsing Hua University",bio:"Bo-Han Lai's Block Reflector Orthogonal Layers and Logit Annealing Loss utilizes low-rank layers and margin-balancing functions to secure neural networks against adversarial attacks. They are currently an MS student and research assistant at National Taiwan University, where they work in the AISLab with Shang-Tse Chen. Their research focuses on improving the adversarial robustness of CV models and developing trustworthy ML systems.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjAzQVFIbnM2ZmVTZ0JaRVEvcHJvZmlsZS1kaXNwbGF5cGhvdG8tc2NhbGVfMjAwXzIwMC9CNTZaZ1I2QzRmSGtBWS0vMC8xNzUyNjQ3MDg2ODAxP2U9MTc4ODk5ODQwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD1zY2RLTWdBNDRRZUpwQVpCMnF1ZXVFMnZVVjd5TGptY3lTdGZtYlVuOWQw",citations:6,hIndex:1,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[187]=["machine learning"],linkedUser:$R[188]={username:"bo-han-lai",name:"Bo-Han Lai"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[189]={id:"01a1fc36-4468-7abb-8697-76d507f7b2dc",role:"CS PhD Student",organization:"National Taiwan University",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"national-taiwan-university",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1NjBCQVFHQWgwOGprV28yM1EvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjc5OTA0NzA4NTUyL25hdGlvbmFsX3RhaXdhbl91bml2ZXJzaXR5X2xvZ28_ZT0xNzk1NjUxMjAwJnY9YmV0YSZ0PTljYnVJYXVNeXMyOUdvNmJUR09fdHczWXg0VVlDRTRya08zVWoyMXZfQ2s"},links:$R[190]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=8-1j8dsAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://bob1113.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bo-han-lai",github:"https://github.com/bob1113",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[191]={full_name:"Kayla Leung",researcher:null},$R[192]={full_name:"Jianping Li",researcher:$R[193]={slug:"jianping-li-2",name:"Jianping Li",affiliation:"Google",headline:"Software Engineer @ Google, Previously CS MSc Student @ University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign",bio:"Jianping Li is a software engineer at Google, building the next-generation agentic browser with Gemini in Chrome. They focus on language agents for real-world automation, connecting product work with research, and are interested in autoresearch and self-improving agents. At Google, they have contributed to integrating SynthID as a tool for the browser agent. Previously, they earned an MS in CS at UIUC and worked with Tong Zhang and Minjia Zhang. They also hold an MS in Robotics from the University of Pennsylvania and a BE in CS from ShanghaiTech University.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9dEh4Y1ViVUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0y",citations:56,hIndex:3,followerCount:5,researchAreas:$R[194]=["Deep Learning","Machine Learning Systems","Machine Learning"],linkedUser:$R[195]={username:"jianping-li",name:"Jianping Li"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[196]={id:"01a1a38d-a26a-7f61-80f4-7cb20336b544",role:"Software Engineer",organization:"Google",location:null,description:"Building the next-generation agentic browser with Gemini in Chrome; contributed to integrating SynthID as a tool for the agent.",organizationSlug:"google",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:4,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q0RTBCQVFHdjNjcU91VU1ZN2cvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvQjRFWm1oZWdYSEdjQU0tLzAvMTc1OTM1MDc1Mzk5MC9nb29nbGVfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9SHphdzBkMFl6MVlpLV9tRHVRNkpRby1QaDQxQUc1MFo4cFdqeWFlVEkwaw"},links:$R[197]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=tHxcUbUAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://jpli02.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jianping-li-b67b1419b",github:"https://github.com/jpli02",twitter:"https://twitter.com/Jasperli0202",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"jplee0202@gmail.com"}}},$R[198]={full_name:"Zhanzhao Li",researcher:$R[199]={slug:"zhanzhao-li",name:"Zhanzhao Li",affiliation:"Rice Academy Postdoctoral Fellow, Rice University",headline:"Rice Academy Postdoctoral Fellow @ Rice University, Previously Civil Engineering PhD Student @ The Pennsylvania State University",bio:"Zhanzhao Li’s Machine learning in concrete science outlines methodological best practices and applications for ML in concrete research. Li is a Rice Academy Postdoctoral Fellow at Rice University, where they also serve as a 2025–2026 Future Faculty Fellow in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering. Their research focuses on construction automation, materials informatics, and the durability of sustainable cementitious materials. Li developed Barbed-wire reinforcement for 3D concrete printing to enhance the structural performance of extrusion-based printed beams. They also authored Fresh and hardened properties of extrusion-based 3D-printed cementitious materials, which reviews the mechanical characteristics and printability of 3D-printed concrete. Li earned a PhD in Civil Engineering with a minor in Computational Materials from The Pennsylvania State University and a BEng from Harbin Institute of Technology.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9dEdpX1RKa0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0xMA",citations:1198,hIndex:10,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[200]=["Cement","Concrete","Durability","Materials informatics","Construction automation"],linkedUser:$R[201]={username:"zhanzhao-li",name:"Zhanzhao Li"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[202]={id:"01a0ad4e-ace9-7bac-9014-c9bbe58369b3",role:"Rice Academy Postdoctoral Fellow",organization:"Rice University",location:"Houston, TX",description:"Working with Kai Gong in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering.",organizationSlug:"rice-university",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M0RTBCQVFHQlc5VWx1WTMtVmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjMwNjAyMjI5NDQ4L3JpY2V1bml2ZXJzaXR5X2xvZ28_ZT0xNzgzNTU1MjAwJnY9YmV0YSZ0PUhvMngzay1FTXNhVUJIZ091ZDBYRUkzS1VvbkZkRTZZUnNYcUtTNGE2Wlk"},links:$R[203]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=tGi_TJkAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://zhanzhaoli.weebly.com/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhanzhaoli",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7674-7424",bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[204]={full_name:"Kazi Mehrab",researcher:$R[205]={slug:"kazi-sajeed-mehrab",name:"Kazi Mehrab",affiliation:"Virginia Tech",headline:"Graduate Research Assistant @ Virginia Tech, Previously Applied Scientist @ Amazon",bio:"Kazi Sajeed Mehrab developed Prompt-cam to increase the interpretability of vision transformers for fine-grained visual analysis. Mehrab is a CS PhD student and Graduate Research Assistant at Virginia Tech focusing on ML and multimodal LLMs. Their research emphasizes visual perception, reasoning, and grounding, particularly through the curation of domain-specific datasets for scientific domains. They also co-created Fish-vista for trait identification from images and VLM4Bio to evaluate vision-language models for biological trait discovery. Prior to their doctoral studies, Mehrab worked on NLP for programming and released CoDesc, a large code-description parallel dataset. They have held research roles at Amazon and LinkedIn and earned a BS from the Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9cmRoM2dWTUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD00",citations:206,hIndex:8,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[206]=["Machine Learning"],linkedUser:$R[207]={username:"kazi-sajeed-mehrab",name:"Kazi Sajeed Mehrab"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[208]={id:"01a030be-6aca-72d9-b2c8-a4a6482d1d7e",role:"Graduate Research Assistant",organization:"Virginia Tech",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"virginia-tech",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2023,startMonth:5,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1MTBCQVFHRW5ISjNPam0xSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjMxMzc1ODg0MjczP2U9MTc4NjU3OTIwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD1IY2xWZmFSV0R3Qy1CR1k5bHVRLUxvam14LU94elo4QjhuUWV6QUpnR1kw"},links:$R[209]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=rdh3gVMAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ksmehrab/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ksmehrab",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[210]={full_name:"Kanwal Mehreen",researcher:$R[211]={slug:"kanwal-mehreen",name:"Kanwal Mehreen",affiliation:"MSCS, UBC",headline:"CS MSc Student @ UBC, Previously Lead NLP Researcher @ Traversaal.ai",bio:"Kanwal Mehreen’s Alif advances Urdu LLMs through multilingual synthetic data distillation. Mehreen is a CS MSc student at UBC advised by Laks V.S. Lakshmanan, where they research LLM behavior, agents, and tool use. They serve as the Geo Regional Asia Lead at Cohere Labs and previously worked as the Lead NLP Researcher at Traversaal.ai curating regional datasets. Their work includes QUAIL, which utilizes quantization-aware unlearning to remove misinformation from LLMs, and methods for the fine-grained detection of AI-generated text. Mehreen also developed 1-800-SHARED-TASKS to detect language and hate speech in Devanagari script languages. They founded the nonprofit FEMCodes and established MITACS Community Pakistan after completing an EE degree at NUST.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9ZHVOQXVKc0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:29,hIndex:4,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[212]=["LLM Post-Training","Multilingual NLP","Adaptive AI"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[213]={id:"01a0ab67-83a6-7da2-81a5-78c241593bf8",role:"CS MSc Student",organization:"UBC",location:"Vancouver, BC",description:"Advised by Prof. Laks V.S. Lakshmanan; researching LLM behavior, agents, and tool use.",organizationSlug:"university-of-british-columbia",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/organization-icons/019ff27c-3b52-748f-a60d-6cd9228d7c41/fd0b52c0-db5a-48a7-bc01-fa8e8e363687/icon.webp"},links:$R[214]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=duNAuJsAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[215]={full_name:"Michael Moor",researcher:$R[216]={slug:"michael-moor",name:"Michael Moor",affiliation:"Assistant Professor at ETH Zurich. Previously: Stanford, Computer Science.",headline:"Assistant Professor, Medical AI @ ETH Zürich, Previously Postdoctoral Scholar @ Stanford University",bio:"Michael Moor co-authored Foundation models for generalist medical artificial intelligence, which describes a framework for building versatile AI systems capable of performing diverse clinical tasks. He is an Assistant Professor at ETH Zurich and previously conducted postdoctoral research in the Computer Science department at Stanford University. An MD PhD, Moor focuses on medical foundation models, LLM agents, and clinical reasoning. He developed Agent Laboratory, a system using LLM agents to automate scientific research workflows, and Med-Flamingo, a multimodal medical few-shot learner. His research also includes Almanac, a RAG system for clinical medicine, and topological ML methods for early disease prediction. Moor completed his PhD at ETH Zurich and earned his medical degree from the University of Basel.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9UV9ZNWNzZ0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD01",citations:10508,hIndex:24,followerCount:8,researchAreas:$R[217]=["Medical AI","Foundation models","LLMs","Agents","Reasoning"],linkedUser:$R[218]={username:"michael-moor",name:"Michael Moor"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[219]={id:"019fcf2f-d113-7168-93b0-395494ac65b7",role:"Assistant Professor, Medical AI",organization:"ETH Zürich",location:"Basel",description:"Tenure-track appointment in the D-BSSE department.",organizationSlug:"eth-zurich",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:9,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M0RDBCQVFIcGtIRHdZaEVvaVEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjMwNTcwNzM2NzgxL2V0aF96dXJpY2hfbG9nbz9lPTE3ODY1NzkyMDAmdj1iZXRhJnQ9Q1ZKWXZ5dDZ5LURhc2VCcUl5RmZuUFJGVUlud0tkVFN2WEZ3cGo1YWJsaw"},links:$R[220]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Q_Y5csgAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.michaelmoor.me/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/michael-moor",github:"https://github.com/mi92",twitter:"https://twitter.com/Michael_D_Moor",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"michael.moor@bsse.ethz.ch"}}},$R[221]={full_name:"Ajinkya Kiran Mulay",researcher:$R[222]={slug:"ajinkya-k-mulay",name:"Ajinkya K Mulay",affiliation:"Research Scientist at Meta, Phd from Purdue University",headline:"Founding AI Research Scientist @ Stealth Startup, Previously Senior Research Scientist @ Meta",bio:"Ajinkya K Mulay created SPriFed-OMP, a sparsifying algorithm that enables exact sparse basis recovery in differentially private federated learning using only 10% of model parameters. Mulay is a Senior Research Scientist at Meta, where they focus on privacy-preserving ML, differential privacy, and safe reasoning models. Their research explores the trade-offs between privacy, scalability, and performance, exemplified by the development of LOCKS for optimal client sampling. In Towards quantifying the carbon emissions, they investigated the environmental costs associated with training differentially private models. Mulay earned a PhD from Purdue University, where they led the ML team for the SuperPower research group. They are an open-source contributor to the PySyft project and a member of the Cohere for AI initiative.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9SDd4NWhZb0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0z",citations:60,hIndex:4,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[223]=["Differential Privacy","Federated Learning","Computational Social Science"],linkedUser:$R[224]={username:"ajinkya",name:"Ajinkya K Mulay"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[225]={id:"01a1f6f2-715f-7888-9aa6-14e1648d37fe",role:"Founding AI Research Scientist",organization:"Stealth Startup",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:10,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[226]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=H7x5hYoAAAAJ",personalSite:"http://thehimalayanleo.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ajinkyamulay",github:"https://github.com/thehimalayanleo",twitter:"https://twitter.com/ajinkya_km",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"http://thehimalayanleo.github.io/cv/",email:"ajinkyamulay123@gmail.com"}}},$R[227]={full_name:"Raj Palleti",researcher:$R[228]={slug:"raj-palleti",name:"Raj Palleti",affiliation:"Stanford University",headline:"Co-Founder @ alphaXiv, Deep Learning Researcher @ Stanford Artificial Intelligence Laboratory (SAIL)",bio:"Raj Palleti’s paper No, to the right enables robots to adjust manipulation tasks in real-time via natural language corrections and shared autonomy. He is a researcher at Stanford University focusing on AI, robotics, and NLP. The No, to the right framework allows robotic systems to integrate online human feedback and dynamically update physical trajectories based on corrective speech. Palleti also developed transfer learning models for predicting myocardial injury from continuous single-lead electrocardiography, published in the Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association. His broader research includes developing shared autonomy systems for natural language supervision, with early methods presented at the ACL Workshop on Learning with Natural Language Supervision. This work focuses on increasing the responsiveness of autonomous agents to human instruction within complex environments.",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/019f906d-0835-7bfc-8df1-5fd616ab6597/7361df96-c7a4-42a7-bef3-7f26c31f6bac/photo.webp",citations:217,hIndex:4,followerCount:35,researchAreas:$R[229]=["AI","Robotics","NLP"],linkedUser:$R[230]={username:"raj",name:"Raj Palleti"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[231]={id:"01a04984-7b1d-722f-9158-23e22e6b08d2",role:"Co-Founder",organization:"alphaXiv",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"alphaxiv",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQWtVa3N3RGpuSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNzM0NTY0MTgwNjE5L2FscGhheGl2X2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PW04S1pRa0RLa2VOempfYUpfeUYtTjBPUldHajZJNTNBX0hsODhMSG9tUk0"},links:$R[232]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=JmmDAJAAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.alphaxiv.org/researchers/raj-palleti",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/raj-palleti/",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:"https://dblp.org/pid/332/8818.html",orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[233]={full_name:"Pouya Sadeghi",researcher:$R[234]={slug:"pouya-sadeghi",name:"Pouya Sadeghi",affiliation:"Computer Science student, University of Waterloo",headline:"Previously CS MSc Student @ University of Waterloo",bio:"Pouya Sadeghi works at the intersection of LLMs, multilingual NLP, and AI safety, focusing on making AI systems more reliable, safe, and inclusive. They are a fellow at Fatima Fellow, where they work on multilingual, multicultural red teaming of LLMs, and an MSc student in CS at the University of Waterloo. Their work includes adapting LLMs to Persian and applying formal methods to safe, trustworthy probabilistic systems. They previously conducted research at Singapore Management University and earned a BSc in Computer Engineering from the University of Tehran. During their undergraduate studies, they won first place in Iran’s national Computer Science student olympiad.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9bFpSTmtyWUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0z",citations:119,hIndex:6,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[235]=[],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[236]={id:"01a1a38d-a00a-75c4-baa8-11f466210e81",role:"CS MSc Student",organization:"University of Waterloo",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"university-of-waterloo",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:9,endYear:2026,endMonth:11,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFIVjQ3MmNuMm5oTXcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvQjU2WmIuSm4yZ0h3QUktLzAvMTc0ODAyMDY1NzkwMC91d2F0ZXJsb29fbG9nbz9lPTE3OTUwNDY0MDAmdj1iZXRhJnQ9VkRhNWJXbzd1YkxINXY5dWRkZ2I3NWNVTmhaMFliakVwZXBibUh4QndSbw"},links:$R[237]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=lZRNkrYAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://ipouyall.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ipouyall",github:"https://github.com/Ipouyall",twitter:"https://twitter.com/Ipouyall",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"pouya.sadeghi@uwaterloo.ca"}}},$R[238]={full_name:"Arth Singh",researcher:$R[239]={slug:"arth-singh",name:"Arth Singh",affiliation:"Research Scientist, AI Safety at AIM Intelligence, South Korea",headline:"Research Scientist AI Safety @ AIM Intelligence, Previously Student @ National Institute of Technology Agartala",bio:"Arth Singh authored Toward Human-AI Complementarity, which evaluates how humans and AI systems collaborate to solve diverse tasks. Singh is a Research Scientist at AIM Intelligence and a Research Assistant at the University of Toronto’s Jinesis Lab. Their research focuses on AI safety, mechanistic interpretability, and adversarial robustness. Singh developed the EgoSafetyBench benchmark for embodied VLMs and studied diffusion model vulnerabilities in Re-Mask and Redirect. They previously performed AI red teaming for Anthropic and held a SPAR Research fellowship. Singh is an undergraduate at the National Institute of Technology Agartala.",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a0a091-b792-738b-988f-d0b3d8999e48/b0136a56-cc17-4374-b7da-554e1f5a7fd3/photo.webp",citations:7,hIndex:2,followerCount:4,researchAreas:$R[240]=["adversarial attacks","adversarial robustness","mechanistic interpretability","chain of thought"],linkedUser:$R[241]={username:"arth",name:"Arth"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[242]={id:"01a0a091-ec51-7e9a-8a8e-be27a9a57e0d",role:"Research Scientist AI Safety",organization:"AIM Intelligence",location:"Seoul, South Korea",description:null,organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:10,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFITjZUUGhBOURDTEEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvQjU2WjExcjVQUUtnQU0tLzAvMTc3NTc5NTkzNDUyMi9haW1faW50ZWxsaWdlbmNlX2NvX2xvZ28_ZT0xNzgzNTU1MjAwJnY9YmV0YSZ0PTA5UGVUSkNILTVjS0NHVlR2b203cGhTOFpOTFFEQnRFZDVwRmdUSEJjSWM"},links:$R[243]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=-vg5SOMAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/arthsingh7in/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/arthsingh7in",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[244]={full_name:"Manan Tayal",researcher:$R[245]={slug:"manan-tayal",name:"Manan Tayal",affiliation:"Research Scientist, Emergence AI",headline:"Research Scientist @ Emergence AI, Previously Visiting Researcher @ Microsoft",bio:"Manan Tayal is a Research Scientist at Emergence AI, where he works on reliable LLM agents for enterprise data tasks. His research focuses on trustworthy autonomy: learning-based decision making that comes with formal safety guarantees. His work spans Hamilton-Jacobi reachability, control barrier functions and safe reinforcement learning. It includes physics-informed learning for safe optimal control, Safe Flow Q-Learning for offline safe RL with flow policies, V-OCBF for learning safety filters from offline data, and stochastic neural control barrier functions. He holds a PhD from the Indian Institute of Science, where he was a Prime Minister's Research Fellow, and a BTech from IIT Bombay.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9aldXUWhZOEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0xNg",citations:423,hIndex:11,followerCount:5,researchAreas:$R[246]=["Trustworthy Autonomy","Safe Control","Offline RL","RLVR","World Models"],linkedUser:$R[247]={username:"manan-tayal",name:"Manan Tayal"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[248]={id:"01a030b1-eb32-7810-971e-c4bbd0e5ef76",role:"Research Scientist",organization:"Emergence AI",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:7,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q0RTBCQVFGSi1zN1lQZjlUTncvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvQjRFWjBfQ2lTUUlzQVktLzAvMTc3NDg3OTEyMzQ1MC9lbWVyZ2VuY2VhaV9sb2dvP2U9MTc4ODk5ODQwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD1EQzN1STFvSGVFcHE4QnQ1NE52Qzk5UzlxQ09IamRvT2VPSXhaOWhPUmlZ"},links:$R[249]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=jWWQhY8AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://manantayal.com/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/manan-tayal",github:"https://github.com/tayalmanan28",twitter:"https://x.com/manantayal_",huggingface:"https://huggingface.co/tayalmanan",openreview:"https://openreview.net/profile?id=%7EManan_Tayal1",dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://manantayal.com/assets/pdf/Manan_Tayal_CV.pdf",email:"tayalmanan28@gmail.com"}}},$R[250]={full_name:"Tao Tu",researcher:$R[251]={slug:"tao-tu",name:"Tao Tu",affiliation:"Columbia University, Google",headline:"Research Scientist @ Google DeepMind, Previously Researcher @ Google",bio:"Large language models encode clinical knowledge is the primary work of Tao Tu, which introduces Med-PaLM for medical question answering and clinical reasoning. He is a researcher at Google and Columbia University focusing on ML for healthcare and neural information processing. His work on Gemini 2.5 advances frontier LLM performance in reasoning, multimodality, and agentic capabilities. Tu’s research also includes Tx-LLM for therapeutic development and the creation of an AI co-scientist to facilitate scientific discovery. He has further explored conversational diagnostic AI and models for accurate differential diagnosis. His earlier studies in multi-modal neuroimaging used EEG-fMRI fusion to analyze macroscale brain dynamics.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9VmxSNnU0QUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0y",citations:25305,hIndex:29,followerCount:11,researchAreas:$R[252]=["multi-modal neuroimaging","machine learning","neural information processing"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[253]={id:"019fd044-0215-7b24-8e40-c665d43799ff",role:"Research Scientist",organization:"Google DeepMind",location:"New York City",description:"Works on Gemini for Science and Health.",organizationSlug:"google-deepmind",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2023,startMonth:4,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q0RTBCQVFFbnRyWXd4UGxiUUEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjkyOTYwNDI1MTg4L2dvb2dsZWRlZXBtaW5kX2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PUl0emNrZjBYUW1iMGNWUUpTS3psbEtsZWF0SDN3SVBnSVJpYXVOOGhaSWM"},links:$R[254]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=VlR6u4AAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[255]={full_name:"Lino Le Van",researcher:$R[256]={slug:"lino-le-van",name:"Lino Le Van",affiliation:"Berkeley",headline:"Co-Founder and CTO @ alphaXiv, Previously EECS Masters Student @ University of California, Berkeley",bio:"Lino Le Van co-founded alphaXiv, which integrates research papers with their corresponding benchmarks and code implementations. They are an EECS MSc student at UC Berkeley and serve as the CTO of the platform. The project focuses on bridging the gap between AI research and practice by surfacing technical artifacts alongside papers. Le Van previously completed an undergraduate degree at UC Santa Cruz. During their time at UCSC, they specialized in systems and database research. Their current work continues to focus on infrastructure that supports the translation of ML research into practical applications.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9SHl0MGowOEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0x",citations:0,hIndex:0,followerCount:17,researchAreas:$R[257]=[],linkedUser:$R[258]={username:"linolevan",name:"Lino Le Van"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[259]={id:"01a03268-baed-73fa-82e4-ffc1d6bddb2e",role:"Co-Founder and CTO",organization:"alphaXiv",location:"San Francisco",description:"Co-founded a platform bringing together papers, benchmarks, and implementations to bridge the AI research-to-practice divide.",organizationSlug:"alphaxiv",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFGQWtVa3N3RGpuSmcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNzM0NTY0MTgwNjE5L2FscGhheGl2X2xvZ28_ZT0yMTQ3NDgzNjQ3JnY9YmV0YSZ0PW04S1pRa0RLa2VOempfYUpfeUYtTjBPUldHajZJNTNBX0hsODhMSG9tUk0"},links:$R[260]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Hyt0j08AAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/linolevan/",github:"https://github.com/lino-levan",twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:"https://bsky.app/profile/linolevan.com",wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[261]={full_name:"Abdul Waheed",researcher:$R[262]={slug:"abdul-waheed",name:"Abdul Waheed",affiliation:"Carnegie Mellon University",headline:"PhD Student @ Carnegie Mellon University",bio:"Abdul Waheed co-created LaMini-LM, a series of distilled models optimized from large-scale instructions. As a Language Technologies MSc student at Carnegie Mellon University, they research robust and interpretable ML, including how dataset variety influences LLM pretraining in On the diversity of synthetic data. Waheed also developed CovidGAN, which uses auxiliary classifier GANs for medical imaging data augmentation. Their speech research includes analyzing hallucinations in foundation models in Lost in Transcription and developing uDistil-Whisper for label-free data filtering. Additionally, they created the GPTAraEval benchmark to evaluate LLMs on Arabic NLP tasks. Waheed’s earlier work investigated speaker-aware learning for dialogue-act classification and analyzed the domain robustness of pretrained language models.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9STBoUmlCWUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0y",citations:2355,hIndex:15,followerCount:3,researchAreas:$R[263]=["Machine Learning"],linkedUser:$R[264]={username:"abdul-waheed",name:"Abdul Waheed"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[265]={id:"01a15a7b-4431-750f-8970-15597dae38a7",role:"PhD Student",organization:"Carnegie Mellon University",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:"cmu",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:8,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1NjBCQVFIMHJNcVd1RGNOekEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjU2NjcwNDMyNzkwL2Nhcm5lZ2llX21lbGxvbl91bml2ZXJzaXR5X2xvZ28_ZT0xNzg2NTc5MjAwJnY9YmV0YSZ0PURyMUlOa3Z1djktampSNjk1cHBUcGRyTWYwbUhsZTJuWjAxdkpzZDRtVHM"},links:$R[266]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=I0hRiBYAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~abdulw/",linkedin:null,github:"https://github.com/macabdul9",twitter:"https://twitter.com/MacAbdul9",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"abdulwaheed1513@gmail.com"}}},$R[267]={full_name:"Fiona Y. Wang",researcher:$R[268]={slug:"fiona-y-wang",name:"Fiona Y Wang",affiliation:"Graduate Student, MIT",headline:"Biological Engineering PhD Student @ Massachusetts Institute of Technology",bio:"Fiona Y Wang co-developed Autonomous agents coordinating distributed discovery, which manages scientific research through the exchange of artifacts between AI agents. Wang is a PhD student in Biological Engineering at MIT and a 2025-2026 MathWorks Fellow. Her research integrates metal coordination, peptide design, and ML to develop programmable materials and atomistic simulations. In Swarms of large language model agents for protein sequence design, she applied LLM ensembles to protein engineering. She also developed Self-Revising Discovery Systems for Science, a categorical framework for agentic AI. Wang previously conducted research at Northwestern University.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9b0xSVkNiVUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD02",citations:88,hIndex:5,followerCount:8,researchAreas:$R[269]=[],linkedUser:$R[270]={username:"fiona-wang",name:"Fiona Wang"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[271]={id:"019feccf-ad32-7030-a1a7-646b534058ba",role:"Biological Engineering PhD Student",organization:"Massachusetts Institute of Technology",location:"Cambridge",description:"Developing programmable, bioinspired materials integrating metal coordination, peptide design, deep learning, and computational modeling.",organizationSlug:"mit",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFILVVYUmZJRElLdWcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjg5Nzk5NzI5MDM1L21pdF9sb2dvP2U9MTc4NjU3OTIwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD16dnR5LXp5eDIzVzV6YnlianpXVExqR2VuS2FXQzJXZDFUbnNDNG5yaC1v"},links:$R[272]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=oLRVCbUAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/fionawang108/",github:null,twitter:"https://x.com/fwang108_",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"fw2@mit.edu"}}},$R[273]={full_name:"Lukas Weidener",researcher:$R[274]={slug:"lukas-weidener",name:"Lukas Weidener",affiliation:"Applied Scientific Intelligence, Inc.",headline:"Co-Founder & Lead Member of Scientific Staff @ Applied Scientific Intelligence, Previously Consultant & Researcher @ Molecule AG",bio:"Lukas Weidener’s Rethinking the AI Scientist uses interactive multi-agent workflows to facilitate scientific discovery. They are a Principal Researcher at Applied Scientific Intelligence, where they focus on AI ethics, medical education, and decentralized science (DeSci). Weidener led a cross-sectional study on AI in medicine to analyze how medical students perceive the technology's ethical applications and educational requirements. They also developed the decentralized science pyramid framework, which applies organizational theory to DeSci research structures. Previously, Weidener held research roles at Bio and Molecule developing blockchain-based scientific platforms and at UMIT Tirol investigating distributed-ledger systems.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9WUlsWm5jUUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD00",citations:906,hIndex:10,followerCount:2,researchAreas:$R[275]=["Science / AI / Ethics"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[276]={id:"01a1132d-5921-7ee3-8060-511df44a45dd",role:"Co-Founder & Lead Member of Scientific Staff",organization:"Applied Scientific Intelligence",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:3,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[277]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=YIlZncQAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[278]={full_name:"Zhen Wu",researcher:null},$R[279]={full_name:"Xuhai “Orson” Xu",researcher:$R[280]={slug:"xuhai-orson-xu",name:"Xuhai \"Orson\" Xu",affiliation:"Assistant Professor, Columbia University | Google",headline:"Assistant Professor, Biomedical Informatics @ Columbia University, Visiting Faculty Researcher @ Google",bio:"Xuhai \"Orson\" Xu's Mental-LLM predicts mental health status by analyzing online text data using LLMs. He is an Assistant Professor of Biomedical Informatics at Columbia University and a Visiting Faculty researcher at Google. His research in HCI and AI focuses on modeling routine human behavior through ubiquitous computing for health applications. Xu also developed MDAgents to facilitate adaptive LLM collaboration for medical decision-making and Health-LLM to predict health outcomes from wearable sensor data. He previously served as a postdoctoral researcher at MIT after completing his PhD at the University of Washington. His earlier work includes the GLOBEM platform for generalizing longitudinal behavior modeling across datasets.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9TXRYNUlqOEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD01",citations:7674,hIndex:41,followerCount:6,researchAreas:$R[281]=["Human-Computer Interaction","Ubiquitous Computing","Human-Centered AI","mHealth","Health Informatics"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[282]={id:"019fcf3b-03ab-7273-80bc-a29c74c63797",role:"Assistant Professor, Biomedical Informatics",organization:"Columbia University",location:"New York, NY",description:"Leads the SEA (Sense, Empower, and Augment) Lab.",organizationSlug:"columbia",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:1,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M0RTBCQVFGeG43OG52VmFUREEvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvMC8xNjMwNjM4NDUyMDQ2L2NvbHVtYmlhX3VuaXZlcnNpdHlfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9Zi0wNTBTcmJ6akVsTXVEcVVGVmhWYVpPWDc5T2pNZHF6NDdiTzZhTGszaw"},links:$R[283]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=MtX5Ij8AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://orsonxu.com/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/orson-xuhai-xu",github:"https://github.com/OrsonXu",twitter:"https://twitter.com/Orson_Xu",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5930-3899",bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://orsonxu.com/files/cv.pdf",email:"xx2489@columbia.edu"}}},$R[284]={full_name:"Dingling Yao",researcher:$R[285]={slug:"dingling-yao",name:"Dingling Yao",affiliation:"PhD student at IST Austria & MPI-IS, Germany",headline:"Visiting Researcher @ Caltech, Doctoral Student @ Institute of Science and Technology Austria",bio:"Dingling Yao’s Multi-view causal representation learning recovers causal factors from multiple views when some variables are unobserved. They are a visiting researcher at Caltech and a doctoral student at IST Austria, after doctoral study at MPI-IS. Their research focuses on causal inference, representation learning, and AI for Science. Other work includes Unifying Causal Representation Learning, which connects causal representations to the invariance principle, and Marrying Causal Representation Learning with Dynamical Systems for Science. Yao earned BA and MSc degrees at the University of Tübingen and has held research roles at AWS and Bosch Center for Artificial Intelligence.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9dk9KVXZiMEFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0xMA",citations:287,hIndex:6,followerCount:3,researchAreas:$R[286]=["AI for Science","Causal Inference","Representation Learning"],linkedUser:$R[287]={username:"dingling-yao",name:"Dingling Yao"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[288]={id:"01a11115-3d62-7c18-b8a7-4de196be6185",role:"Visiting Researcher",organization:"Caltech",location:"Pasadena, CA",description:null,organizationSlug:"caltech",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:4,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1MTBCQVFGQ0dxRW1Td3JjNHcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvMC8xNjMxMzM4OTk0MzY5P2U9MTc4NjU3OTIwMCZ2PWJldGEmdD1Ec1d2WU5RbDlLZWRkRWJnbmwwZ1pYODdrTG1JMEU0aEpyb1dsU2NQOVNB"},links:$R[289]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=vOJUvb0AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://dinglingyao.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/dingling-yao",github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"dingling.yao@ista.ac.at"}}},$R[290]={full_name:"Rojin Ziaei",researcher:$R[291]={slug:"rojin-ziaei",name:"Rojin Ziaei",affiliation:"Researcher@Stanford",headline:"Research Biostatistician II @ Stanford University, CS MSc Student @ Georgetown University",bio:"Rojin Ziaei is a biostatistician in social epidemiology at Stanford’s Center for Population Health Sciences, using LLM-based social simulations to predict population health behavior. They helped build AgentClinic, a multimodal benchmark for evaluating AI agents in simulated clinical settings. Their work on The Limits of Simulated Societies examines how LLM alignment can erase cross-cultural differences. They also study medical LLM bias and self-diagnosis, Persian and other low-resource language technologies, and fairness in hiring and lending. Ziaei is pursuing an MS in computer science at Georgetown University and previously worked in research at Stanford, Johns Hopkins, and the University of Maryland, where they earned a BS in information science.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9aGhYdTZqa0FBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD00",citations:866,hIndex:6,followerCount:3,researchAreas:$R[292]=["Social Simulation","Computational Social Science","Fairness in AI","Culturally aware AI"],linkedUser:null,takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[293]={id:"01a1a388-95fc-7418-810a-85815cf4e40c",role:"Research Biostatistician II",organization:"Stanford University",location:"Palo Alto, CA",description:"Develops LLM-based social simulations alongside classical NLP and machine learning using electronic health records and long-form narrative data.",organizationSlug:"stanford",isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:9,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0M1NjBCQVFIcjlzdXh5SkJYTXcvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzEwMF8xMDAvMC8xNjM1NTM0Mzc4ODcwL3N0YW5mb3JkX3VuaXZlcnNpdHlfbG9nbz9lPTIxNDc0ODM2NDcmdj1iZXRhJnQ9WnZCMjVMOTVvOXc0cTlkcnZzV3hHY000OXRYNjZDZjVMc0xBeFlwOHJTcw"},links:$R[294]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=hhXu6jkAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://rojinziaei.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rojin-ziaei-549725a5",github:"https://github.com/RojinZiaei",twitter:"https://twitter.com/rojin_ziaei",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://rojinziaei.github.io/cv.pdf",email:"rziaei@stanford.edu"}}},$R[295]={full_name:"Boyang Zhong",researcher:$R[296]={slug:"boyang-zhong",name:"Boyang Zhong",affiliation:"Technical University of Munich (TUM)",headline:"Research Intern @ Agile Robots SE, Student Researcher (CVG Group) @ Technical University of Munich (TUM)",bio:"Boyang Zhong's A Very Big Video Reasoning Suite evaluates complex reasoning capabilities within large-scale video datasets. Zhong is a researcher at the Technical University of Munich. Their research focuses on embodied AI, multimodal learning, and 3D Computer Vision. They developed Funcanon to enable generalizable robotic manipulation through functional object canonicalization and pose-aware action primitives. Zhong also authored Pose Anything Anywhere, which performs model-free object pose estimation using arbitrary references. Their work has appeared at venues including ICML, ICRA, and ECCV.",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/01a030e5-512e-742d-b630-3a42fcb5bbd2/48e9989f-e821-4b15-a21d-9c4ec136c81e/photo.webp",citations:33,hIndex:2,followerCount:3,researchAreas:$R[297]=["Embodied AI","Interactive World Modeling","Spatial Intelligence"],linkedUser:$R[298]={username:"boyang-zhong",name:"伯扬 钟"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[299]={id:"01a033cb-425c-7ca5-be95-942a958536a1",role:"Research Intern",organization:"Agile Robots SE",location:"Munich, Germany",description:"Working on Contact-aware World Action Model for Dexterous Manipulation of Humanoids",organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2026,startMonth:6,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:null},links:$R[300]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=VI0i7c0AAAAJ",personalSite:"https://andzy324.github.io/",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/boyang-zhong/",github:"https://github.com/Andzy324",twitter:null,huggingface:"https://huggingface.co/AndZHONG",openreview:"https://openreview.net/profile?id=%7EBoyang_ZHONG3",dblp:null,orcid:"https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7827-7958",bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:"boyang.zhong@tum.de"}}},$R[301]={full_name:"Haotian Zong",researcher:$R[302]={slug:"haotian-zong",name:"Haotian Zong",affiliation:"Johns Hopkins University, Department of Applied Mathematics and Statistics",headline:"Applied Mathematics and Statistics PhD Student @ Johns Hopkins Whiting School of Engineering, Previously Statistics and Economics BS Student @ University of Chicago",bio:"Haotian Zong is a PhD student in applied mathematics and statistics at Johns Hopkins, studying decision-making under uncertainty and human-AI interaction. They are also a graduate research assistant at the Whiting School of Engineering. Zong studied statistics and economics at the University of Chicago, where they completed undergraduate research in computer science, business, political science, and public policy. Their experience also includes a computer vision software engineering internship and a data science internship.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9UnBLQi0xSUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD00",citations:45,hIndex:3,followerCount:2,researchAreas:$R[303]=["Decision Making under Uncertainty","Human-AI Interaction"],linkedUser:$R[304]={username:"haotian-zong",name:"Haotian Zong"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[305]={id:"01a18104-3cfa-7524-b04b-bc96ba193d0b",role:"Applied Mathematics and Statistics PhD Student",organization:"Johns Hopkins Whiting School of Engineering",location:null,description:null,organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2024,startMonth:null,endYear:2029,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv."},links:$R[306]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=RpKB-1IAAAAJ",personalSite:null,linkedin:null,github:null,twitter:null,huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:null,bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:null,email:null}}},$R[307]={full_name:"Markus J. Buehler",researcher:$R[308]={slug:"markus-j-buehler",name:"Markus J. Buehler",affiliation:"Massachusetts Institute of Technology",headline:"Co-Founder & CTO @ Unreasonable Labs, McAfee Professor of Engineering @ Massachusetts Institute of Technology",bio:"Markus J. Buehler’s Nanoconfinement in silk explains how the specific size of protein crystals provides spider silk with its extreme mechanical toughness. He is the McAfee Professor of Engineering at MIT and serves as the Co-Founder and CTO of Unreasonable Labs. His research integrates ML with materials science to model and design bioinspired structures, including collagen, bone, and advanced composites. Through Molecular model of cement hydrates, he established an atomistic understanding of the chemical building blocks of construction materials. Buehler’s recent work involves developing graph-aware multi-agent AI systems to automate knowledge discovery in nanotechnology and protein science. He previously served as the head of MIT’s Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and earned his PhD from the Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems.",photoUrl:"https://user.assets.alphaxiv.org/researcher-photos/019f66b0-82de-7f99-ba73-594fc5ce6f00/275b521b-802c-4de7-962c-99ee35489e83/photo.webp",citations:67001,hIndex:132,followerCount:12,researchAreas:$R[309]=["Materials science","artificial intelligence","biomaterials","bioinspiration","failure"],linkedUser:$R[310]={username:"markus-j-buehler",name:"Markus J. Buehler"},takenDown:!1,topAffiliation:$R[311]={id:"019fcecd-3960-7e01-9217-105f61806ce3",role:"Co-Founder & CTO",organization:"Unreasonable Labs",location:null,description:"Building AI systems that generate novel scientific knowledge and actionable insight across materials science, biology, and healthcare.",organizationSlug:null,isHeadlineWorthy:!0,startYear:2025,startMonth:1,endYear:null,endMonth:null,logoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9tZWRpYS5saWNkbi5jb20vZG1zL2ltYWdlL3YyL0Q1NjBCQVFIQzZjTG1MRUVWZncvY29tcGFueS1sb2dvXzIwMF8yMDAvQjU2WnYuVi56bEhRQU0tLzAvMTc2OTQ5ODczNDM1OC91bnJlYXNvbmFibGVfbGFic19sb2dvP2U9MjE0NzQ4MzY0NyZ2PWJldGEmdD13RHhSVUp5Qms3eEsxc0pMWjUyMnVEdEpySF9pdjFjZ2dMQVB6Vk5PcVFN"},links:$R[312]={scholar:"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=hWBTSksAAAAJ",personalSite:"https://meche.mit.edu/people/faculty/mbuehler@mit.edu",linkedin:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/markus-j-buehler-2245682",github:null,twitter:"https://twitter.com/ProfBuehlerMIT",huggingface:null,openreview:null,dblp:null,orcid:"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4173-9659",bluesky:null,wikipedia:null,cv:"https://meche.mit.edu/sites/default/files/cv/Markus_Buehler-biosketch_0.pdf",email:"mbuehler@mit.edu"}}},$R[313]={full_name:"Samuel Schmidgall",researcher:$R[314]={slug:"samuel-schmidgall",name:"Samuel Schmidgall",affiliation:"Google DeepMind",headline:"Research Scientist @ Google DeepMind, Previously PhD Student @ The Johns Hopkins University",bio:"Samuel Schmidgall is a Research Scientist at Google DeepMind focusing on AI for science, medical AI, and surgical robotics. Schmidgall completed his PhD at Johns Hopkins University in January 2026. Schmidgall led the development of Agent Laboratory, an LLM agent framework that automates the research process from initial ideas to code repositories and reports, worked on MedGemma, a suite of medical vision-language models, and TxGemma, which uses agentic LLMs for therapeutic property prediction. His work on autonomous surgery includes SRT-H, a hierarchical framework for imitation learning, and the SRT transformer for surgical subtasks. He also introduced AgentClinic as a multimodal benchmark for clinical agents and AgentRxiv to facilitate collaborative autonomous research. Schmidgall previously held research roles at Stanford University and AMD.",photoUrl:"https://proxy.assets.alphaxiv.org/aHR0cHM6Ly9zY2hvbGFyLmdvb2dsZXVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbS9jaXRhdGlvbnM_dmlld19vcD12aWV3X3Bob3RvJnVzZXI9YlFEb29aRUFBQUFKJmNpdHBpZD0xMw",citations:5151,hIndex:23,followerCount:341,resea